# Rebuild & Reload after runtime-affecting changes

When you change code or config that the **running** LLAAB server or client will not pick up via HMR alone, you **must** trigger a rebuild/reload before telling the user to verify in the browser.

## When to trigger (required)

Run Rebuild & Reload after changing any of:

- `apps/server/**` (routes, middleware, `index.ts`, lib helpers)
- `packages/**` consumed by the server (`@llaab/core`, `@llaab/ingestion`, `@llaab/skills`, `@llaab/llm`, `@llaab/schemas`, `@llaab/control`, …)
- Root `.env` / `.env.example` values the server reads at process start
- Anything that only takes effect after a server restart (Bun idle timeouts, git helpers, enrich, vault routes, auth, etc.)

Client-only UI under `apps/client/**` usually hot-reloads; still reload if the change depends on a rebuilt workspace package or a restarted API.

## How to trigger

Prefer the same path as SwiftBar **Rebuild & Reload App**:

```bash
mkdir -p "$HOME/Library/Logs/llaab"
./scripts/macos/dev-refresh.sh
```

If `dev-refresh.sh` fails, fall back to restarting the server (and client if needed):

```bash
./scripts/macos/llaab-service.sh stop-server
./scripts/macos/llaab-service.sh start-server
# and/or stop-client / start-client
```

Do **not** assume the user will click SwiftBar. Agents own the reload when their changes require it.

## After reload

- Confirm the server is up (e.g. `llaab-service.sh status` or a quick health/API check).
- Only then ask the user to hard-refresh the browser and verify.
